<title>FRANCE: EU votes regulation on malting barley quota - ONIC.</title>
<headline>EU votes regulation on malting barley quota - ONIC.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday voted a regulation for the introduction of an import quota for 30,000 tonnes of malting barley, France's grain office ONIC said. Futher details were not immediately available.</p>
<p>The reduced-tariff import quota has been tied to a lengthy dispute between the United States and the EU over the introduction of a new EU rice import quota system allowing three month cumulative recovery of overpaid duties.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
